# LF in the repository on every platform.
#
# Windows CI runners default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF. The registry generator writes LF and byte-compares its output
# against what is committed, so without this the freshness check fails on
# Windows and only on Windows — which is exactly how it was found.
#
# Making that comparison line-ending-insensitive would have hidden real drift,
# so the repository enforces the invariant instead of the check tolerating its
# absence. Golden reporter output and code-frame fixtures depend on it too.
* text=auto eol=lf
